\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. When quiet in my house I sit,
\par Thy Book be my companion still,
\par My joy Thy sayings to repeat,
\par Talk o'er the records of Thy will,
\par And search the oracles divine,
\par Till every heartfelt word be mine.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. O may the gracious words divine
\par Subject of all my converse be!
\par So will the Lord His follower join,
\par And walk and talk Himself with me;
\par So shall my heart His presence prove,
\par And burn with everlasting love.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Oft as I lay me down to rest,
\par O may the reconciling word
\par Sweetly compose my weary breast!
\par While, on the bosom of my Lord,
\par I sink in blissful dreams away,
\par And visions of eternal day.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Rising to sing my Saviour's praise,
\par Thee may I publish all day long;
\par And let Thy precious word of grace
\par Flow from my heart, and fill my tongue;
\par Fill join me to the Church above.
\par                                          Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
